{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan review PASS on round 2 (round 1 was BLOCK).\n\nRound-1 blocking finding, fixed: the plan changed `make test`'s scheduler without\nenumerating the docs that describe its serial behaviour. Now enumerated —\ndocs/local-dev-env.md:466 and docs/coverage.md:36-47 are updated; docs/local-dev-env.md:470-483\nis reviewed and deliberately left (it contrasts coverage tracing and tier breadth, not\nscheduling, and already quotes `-n 4 --dist worksteal`).\n\nRound-1 advisories that corrected the reasoning, also fixed:\n- DEFAULT_SUITE_MARKS is matrix-CONDITIONAL, not the flat string the plan claimed. Restated:\n  `make test` exactly matches the gating ubuntu-latest/py3.13 cell, is a strict superset of\n  the other two Ubuntu cells (`... and not repo_policy`), and a superset of the macOS\n  platform_compat subset. The completeness-by-construction argument survives, now accurately.\n- The repo has an explicit reasoned decision AGAINST `-n auto` (_build-and-test.yml:780:\n  'over-subscribes on larger local hosts'), and docs/coverage.md:42-47 already recommends\n  `-n 4 --dist worksteal` locally. The plan's `-n auto` contradicted both; it is now\n  `-n $(PYTEST_WORKERS) --dist worksteal`, PYTEST_WORKERS ?= 4.\n- An AC recorded a one-time measurement rather than a durable end-state; it is now\n  '`make verify`'s help text states its measured cost', which is observable in the tree.\n\nScheduler measurement on this host (18 logical / 6 performance cores, worktree venv):\n- `-n auto` (= 18 workers): 7% in ~8 min, extrapolating past 100 min. Oversubscribes badly\n  because a large share of this suite forks git/bash/pytest subprocesses of its own. This is\n  direct empirical confirmation of the repo's existing anti-auto decision.\n- `-n 4 --dist worksteal` (CI's ubuntu pin): tracking to ~16 min on a clean tree.\n- serial, from the ticket corpus: 1726 s (~29 min).\nSo parallel-at-4 is the documented default, not an optimisation the reader must discover."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788514442955256001,"uuid":"ce6d1840-f93e-4454-ac83-48654cc5d53b"}